---
import ContentLayout from "../../layouts/ContentLayout.astro";
---

<ContentLayout
  title="Watch Multiple YouTube Live Streams at Once | Stream Mix"
  description="Arrange multiple YouTube live streams and live chats in one customizable browser grid with Stream Mix."
  heading="Watch multiple YouTube live streams at once"
>
  <p>
    Use Stream Mix to arrange several YouTube broadcasts in one browser page.
    You can keep an official event feed beside alternate perspectives, creator
    coverage, or separate live chats.
  </p>
  <h2>Find the YouTube video ID</h2>
  <p>
    In a standard YouTube URL, the video ID is the value after
    <code>watch?v=</code>. Enter that value in Stream Mix, choose the display
    mode, and add the window to your grid.
  </p>
  <h2>Using YouTube live chat</h2>
  <p>
    Chat is available only when the video is live and its creator has enabled
    live chat. Recorded videos, scheduled broadcasts, made-for-kids content, and
    streams with disabled chat may show an unavailable message.
  </p>
  <p>
    For mixed-platform events, read the complete
    <a href="/guides/watch-multiple-streams">multistream viewing guide</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    <a href="/" class="btn btn-primary">Open the YouTube multistream viewer</a>
  </p>
</ContentLayout>
